# Sidecar ignore file for ops/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit convention: a file named `<dockerfile-filename>.dockerignore`
# placed next to a Dockerfile overrides the root `.dockerignore` for builds
# using that Dockerfile. Because ops/docker-compose.yml sets
# `build.context: ..` (repo root) and `build.dockerfile: ops/Dockerfile`,
# this file - not a root-level .dockerignore - is what controls what reaches
# the build context for this image.
#
# DO NOT add any pattern here that excludes `server/` or its subpaths. The
# Dockerfile COPYs from server/ (package.json, package-lock.json,
# server/packages/*, and the full server/. tree in the build stage) - doing
# so would silently produce an empty or broken image with no clear error.

# Version control and repo metadata - not needed inside the image.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Docs and non-server top-level content - irrelevant to the Node build.
README.md
docs
firmware
ops
data

# Local build artifacts / dependency caches on the host. These are always
# regenerated inside the image by `npm ci` / `npm run build`, so shipping
# host copies would only bloat the build context and risk stale artifacts
# leaking into a stage that expects a clean install.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

# Editor / OS cruft.
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
